- Feedback at `feedback/tmp102/prompt2d.md`

**Chip behaviour (essentials for the test_spec)**
- I²C slave on address `0x48` (ADD0 low) / `0x49` (ADD0 high).
- `temperature` float attribute (default 21.0 °C) encoded into the 12-bit two's-complement Temperature Register (`0x00`), refreshed on each read so the live control takes effect.
- Pointer register (P1:P0 only), MSB-first 16-bit read/write with auto-increment across all 4 registers.
- Registers: Temp (`0x00`, read-only), Configuration (`0x01` reset `0x6180`), TLOW (`0x02` reset `0x04B0`), THIGH (`0x03` reset `0x0500`).
- ALERT left floating; excluded features (alarm thresholds, extended/high-speed/general-call, one-shot, conversion-rate, fault queue) not implemented.
